            <ArticleTitle>Tornwaldt's cyst presenting only as occipital headache: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2008.01186.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tornwaldt's cyst (sometimes called Thornwaldt's cyst) is a rare cause of occipital headache. Owing to the rare occurrence of occipital headache as a symptom of Tornwaldt's cyst, if the patient presented only with occipital headache, this clinical symptom may be falsely perceived as a sign of neurologic disease leading to time-consuming diagnostic examinations that delay the establishment of a correct diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
